Workers static assets don't have a "base path" or "mount prefix" setting. Cloudflare's [Serving a subdirectory guide](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/routing/advanced/serving-a-subdirectory/) has you create a `docs/` folder inside your assets directory. To skip that, have your Worker handle `/docs/*` requests itself: strip the prefix and fetch the file through the `ASSETS` binding.

**wrangler.jsonc**
```jsonc
{
  "name": "my-worker",
  "main": "src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-01",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./public",          // files stay where they are
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "run_worker_first": ["/docs/*"]   // send /docs requests to the Worker first
  }
}
```

**src/index.ts**
```ts
export default {
  async fetch(request, env): Promise<Response> {
    const url = new URL(request.url);

    if (url.pathname === "/docs") {
      return Response.redirect(`${url.origin}/docs/`, 301);
    }

    if (url.pathname.startsWith("/docs/")) {
      url.pathname = url.pathname.slice("/docs".length); // /docs/a/b.html -> /a/b.html
      return env.ASSETS.fetch(new Request(url, request));
    }

    return new Response("Not found", { status: 404 });
  },
} satisfies ExportedHandler<{ ASSETS: Fetcher }>;
```

Things to watch:
- **Unprefixed URLs still work.** Requests that skip the Worker still match assets at their real paths, so `/index.html` would load without `/docs`. To stop that, set `"run_worker_first": true` so every request goes through the Worker, and return 404 for anything outside `/docs/`.
- **Links inside the files.** The Worker only changes how URLs map to files. It doesn't edit the HTML. Root-absolute links like `/style.css` will request the unprefixed path, so use relative links or set your generator's base path. Examples: Vite `base: "/docs/"`, Astro `base`, Docusaurus `baseUrl`.
- **Redirects from the asset server.** Its own redirects, such as `/foo.html` to `/foo`, send back a `Location` without the prefix. If that matters, rewrite the `Location` header on 3xx responses so it starts with `/docs`.
- **Version.** Passing a list of patterns to `run_worker_first` needs a fairly recent Wrangler, so update if it fails to parse. I checked Ludion first and it had no lessons on this.

If you don't mind the layout changing only in the build output, another option is a build step that writes into `dist/docs/`. Your source files stay where they are, and you can use Cloudflare's documented subdirectory method without writing Worker code.

Sources:
- [Serving a subdirectory – Cloudflare Docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/routing/advanced/serving-a-subdirectory/)
- [Static Assets configuration and bindings – Cloudflare Docs](https://docs.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/binding/)

